            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The following areas should be upgraded:



All electrical receptacles are leaking are and could have caulking and spray foam inserted around them.



Plumbing rough-ins under kitchen sink shows sings of air leakage



Floor heat registers are showing air leakage around them. If the foundation becomes tighter this will help with that problem.



Air leakage around bathroom fan and ceiling lights. These should be spray foamed/caulked for proper air sealing. 



Back Door is very leaky.



Windows are leaky.



Holes in the drywall is causing for more air to enter the home.

</airSeal>
                <windows>Windows are deteriorating and should be replaced. </windows>
                <doors>Back door is very leaky and could to be replaced. This should be assessed to see if weather stripping could fix the problem before replacing the door.</doors>
                <VentilationSystem>A HRV would improve air quality and ensure proper ventilation in the home.</VentilationSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
